  "component": {
    "same_space": "h : TGLExt.ImportedSQ.H1, existing orbitalMeasure0, existing lowerProfileWave and realProfileWave. No new physical representation.",
    "main_hypothesis": "RegularProfile h = all existing polynomial energy L1 moments. The proof of integrability consumes existing profileWaveIntegrand_integrable. The StrongRegularProfile corollary uses only hh.1. No generator-domain or charge identity hypothesis is added.",
    "integrand_identity": "wavePhase*x lowerDensity(0,a+2) + wavePhase*x lowerDensity(1,a+2) = shellNullFrequency • (wavePhase * sum_j nullPolarization[a,j]*h_j). Derived from the existing null_strength_factor and lowered metric signs.",
    "integrability": "The sum of the two integrable lowered Maxwell components is integrable; exact pointwise equality gives integrability of the u-weighted phase/amplitude. It discharges the hypothesis of orbital_nullFrequency_bochner_cancel.",
    "transport": "lowerProfileWave(0,a+2,x)+lowerProfileWave(1,a+2,x) = integral_q integral_{u>0} wavePhase(x,y(q,u))*sum_j P(y(q,u))[a,j]*h(y(q,u))_j, where y=(q,(r(q)^2-u^2)/(2u)).",
    "phase": "At x=(lambda,lambda,z0,z1), wavePhase=exp(i*(-u*lambda+q0*z0+q1*z1)); proved using the existing metricFlip_inner and null_inverseLongitudinal.",
    "real_wave": "realProfileWave(0,a+2,x)+realProfileWave(1,a+2,x) = realWaveProjection(nullAngularWave h a lambda z). Existing sqrt(2) real projection is preserved.",
    "polarization": "The source also states by definitional equality that nullPolarization(y(q,u)) is independent of u.",
    "normalization": "nullAngularWave is raw angular Fourier with no prefactor. The previously compiled calibrated stress is unchanged.",
    "domain": "All lambda,z and screen a:Fin2; u integration restricted Ioi0. The transverse zero axis is handled by the imported Bochner theorem, not a new physical hypothesis."
  },
